# Install scripts (`install.ps1`, `install.sh`)

## Requirements

- Idempotent; no admin; user-level `uv tool install`
- Resolve package from latest GitHub release tag (not raw branch URLs)
- Never overwrite existing host config at `~/.sentinel-ai/config.toml`

**PowerShell:** `#Requires -Version 5.1`, `$ErrorActionPreference = "Stop"`, check `$LASTEXITCODE` after `uv` / `sentinel-ai`.

**Bash:** `set -euo pipefail`; ensure `~/.local/bin` and `~/.cargo/bin` on PATH after uv install.

## One-liners (latest release)

```powershell
irm https://github.com/mhdrezky/sentinel-ai/releases/latest/download/install.ps1 | iex
```

```bash
curl -fsSL https://github.com/mhdrezky/sentinel-ai/releases/latest/download/install.sh | bash
```

## Install source

Resolve tag from `GET /repos/mhdrezky/sentinel-ai/releases/latest`, then:

```text
uv tool install --force "git+https://github.com/mhdrezky/sentinel-ai.git@<tag>"
```

Local dev: `uv tool install --force --from <path> sentinel-ai`

## Remote piping

Parameters do not pass through pipe. Optional local source via env var:

```powershell
$env:SENTINEL_SOURCE = "D:\path\to\sentinel-ai"
irm …/releases/latest/download/install.ps1 | iex
```

```bash
SENTINEL_SOURCE=/path/to/sentinel-ai curl -fsSL …/install.sh | bash
```

Or `bash install.sh --source /path/to/sentinel-ai` when invoking the script directly.

## Host config

Fetch `sentinel.toml` from the **same release tag** as the package install.
Fallback heredoc must stay in sync with `src/sentinel_ai/sentinel.toml`.
Never overwrite existing host config.
